ividual and so the gsb is a  need-based institution and there was  lots of reasons why we went to need base  but we did have three guiding principles  that we wanted to achieve with whatever  financial aid system that we  um implemented and so the first one was  excellence no matter what we chose  we still wanted to deliver the best  class possible right an excellent  diverse class the next one was access  so the student whoever you know receives  financial aid  or is coming to the gsb has this can  have the same experience  um as anyone else so there's a access to  the educational experience  uh and then overwhelmingly when we  reached out to community members like  students  uh and staff and faculty and alumni  the idea of fairness was really  important to the gsb  everyone everyone who's admitted has  worked so  hard to get into the gsb that they  should have the same  opportunity for aid and there's a fair  and transparent  process and so when we boiled all that  up it really  overwhelmingly was a need-based system  and although merit is great the  need-based system really serves the  the mission and the purpose of the gsb  um and then  you know as just a side note what we  also loved about a need-based process  and ebay system  was the overall indebtedness of the  students once they left the gsb  because when you you're awarding aid in  a need-based system you're awarding it  to the neediest  students um and so you find that the  indebtedness overall  of the institution is driven down as  well so there's  those were the main reasons the main  principles of why we chose an ebay  system  and so obviously you know the it's our  new base system is going to be going to  the needs of students  um can you tell me more about kind of  like what are other opportunities  students use to  um to fund their mba uh while they're at  uh the gsb  yeah so um the i mean the main source  of funding that we offer is the  fellowship funding which is based on  that need-based system 