p  and so the biggest difference between  the bold fellowship and the need-based  uh fellowship is the bold really  assesses your your family's  financial need not just your individual  financial aid so it's one  step uh it's one step further to  understand the full financial picture  for you and your family and it's similar  to the need based process you apply once  you're admitted  and then will uh notify you for bold or  for the need-based fellowship  at the same time and  so what would happen if the financial  situation of a student changes  um in the you know it's a two-year  program what if something happens  changes in the middle of it that's  common  right i mean with a need-based system it  really is your  individual need and your financial  situation and we do  often see that it can change but from  the time that you're admitted  to sometimes in the middle of your  program and so  we we have avenues for you to report  this new information to us  because we do want to know when your  financial situation changes  so we can reassess your overall  financial strength  and you really we can do this at any  point when you're you're  a student at the gsb so there's there's  ways to report that information to us  and we encourage our students to do that  because it's  you know applying before your you accept  your admissions  offer doesn't mean you're in the same  financial situation once you've  matriculated so there's that open  channel of communication throughout your  entire program  that's great so you know a question that  i feel like we get a lot  um you know we have people in armed  services  from around the world um coming to gsb  um  and in particular in the us there are  programs like uh the gi bill yellow  ribbon  um could you walk through the for us in  the crowd  kind of what that means and uh what the  gsp does with that yeah so  the gsb is a yellow ribbon approved  school  um so this is chapter 33 with yellow  ribbon  and so our our benefit for our 