d to be very uh underutilized  you know at the gsb but also elsewhere  and that's because  the process to apply for an external  scholarship and this is really  any scholarship outside of the gsb  independent of our fellowship through  other organizations uh the process to  obtain  external scholarships can feel tedious  um  but the the cycles in which they award  external scholarships  for let's say next fall if you  matriculate next fall is right now these  scholarship  applications are open now so even though  you're not admitted this is the time  when you want to start  looking for external scholarships  because we do allow you to bring those  into the gsb to help supplement  you know any loans that you may need to  take or any other  contributions so we have some resources  right now on the public website we  actually have a list of external  scholarships that are available  that list is very specific to students  who have received  these memberships at our university so  don't limit yourself to that list use it  as a jumping off point that's where you  want to start  but definitely don't limit yourself to  it and start applying now like now's the  time to do it because once you're  admitted  and then you're thinking about it maybe  over the summer before you actually  matriculate at the gsb  those applications are already closed  for the upcoming academic year  so now is the perfect time to really  start exploring that  and then finally one thing that i talk  about a lot with students  is really budgeting and understanding  what the cost of attendance means  because the cost of attendance you can  find on our website  and for any institution really what a  cost of attendance is made up of  is direct and indirect costs and a  direct cost is something that the  university  will directly bill you for like tuition  like fees you know those things that you  have to pay  but the cost of attendance is also built  around indirect costs  and indirect costs are you know