ease disbursement to the  university so there's  lots of different ways that you can  approach how you lend and the great  thing the great conversations we  actually have with our students  is really around strategy lending  strategy  at what time during the academic year do  you need to borrow  at what amount do you actually need to  borrow and that goes back to those  indirect and direct costs  so there's lots of lots of different  ways to approach it but we're here to  walk you through that process  okay great um another great question i  saw come through  is how are the a student's  admissions decision and their need tied  are they taking into consideration  either way at the financial situation  it's not it's actually not tied at all  so the admissions process is completely  need blind  so you apply for financial aid after  you've been admitted  so there there's no correlation at all  it's completely independent which  you know really ties back to the  fairness um that we wanted to establish  with the need-based  program where everyone who's admitted  worked so hard to get admitted  should have the same opportunity for aid  and that comes after you've been  admitted into the program  great and we're getting here on time so  i am going to ask  one last question from the group um so  we've got someone here it looks like  they're a little farther out from  applying and they're asking what should  they start doing  to prepare financially uh for their mba  in the coming year before they apply  yeah i want to bring it back again to  the external  scholarships this is the time that you  want to start looking  and researching external opportunities  now  um that again that's one of the most  under utilized forms of financial aid  and the application cycles for external  scholarships  are always from the year prior so  students who may be matriculating fall  of 2021  should start applying for external  scholarships now  otherwise if you wait too long it will  close so t